{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide takes you from a wired Swidux app to fully-tracked user behavior with screen views, action-driven events, identity management, opt-out support, and shutdown flushing. It covers state and action wiring, implementing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", declaring an event mapper, configuring auto-identify, and flushing on app background.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference of every type and action, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","isActive":true},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Before you start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a Swidux app already wired up — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have an analytics backend in mind. Mixpanel is the path of least resistance via the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" companion package, but Amplitude, PostHog, Segment, or a custom backend work just as well — the plugin doesn’t care."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxAnalytics\",","    ]",")"]},{"anchor":"Step-2-Add-state-and-actions","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 2: Add state and actions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add an analytics slice to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and an analytics case to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppState.swift","import SwiduxAnalytics","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var analytics: AnalyticsState = .init()","    \/\/ … other slices","}"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppAction.swift","import SwiduxAnalytics","","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case analytics(AnalyticsAction)","    \/\/ … other cases","}"]},{"style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxAnalytics"},{"text":" is needed in ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"text":" file that touches ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.analytics.*"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsAction"},{"text":" — including views that read the slice for display. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin owns reducing for ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" actions, so the root reducer should fall through:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ AppReducer.swift","case .analytics:","    return nil"]},{"anchor":"Step-3-Provide-an-AnalyticsService","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 3: Provide an `AnalyticsService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that talks to your analytics backend. Pick the path that matches your backend.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Path-A-Mixpanel-recommended","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Path A: Mixpanel (recommended)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","isActive":true},{"text":" companion package and use the supplied ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No bridging code on your side.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","","let service = MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"your-mixpanel-token\")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See the package’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","isActive":true},{"text":" for configuration details.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Path-B-Amplitude--PostHog--Segment--custom-backend","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Path B: Amplitude \/ PostHog \/ Segment \/ custom backend"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For any non-Mixpanel backend, implement ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly. The protocol is small:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxAnalytics","","struct MyAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    func track(_ event: AnalyticsEvent) async {","        \/\/ Forward event.name + event.properties to your SDK.","    }","","    func identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]) async {","        \/\/ Set the active user and people properties.","    }","","    func alias(newID: String, previousID: String?) async {","        \/\/ Link an anonymous distinct ID to a known user ID.","    }","","    func reset() async {","        \/\/ Clear local identity (logout). Subsequent events should be anonymous.","    }","","    func flush() async {","        \/\/ Drain in-flight buffers (called by the plugin on app shutdown).","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Translate ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cases (","type":"text"},{"code":".string","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".date","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".dict","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") into whatever your SDK takes. The mapping is mechanical: each case has an obvious target type.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Previews-and-tests","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Previews and tests"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the built-in ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for backend-agnostic previews:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let service = MockAnalyticsService()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re on Path A, ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ships ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for Mixpanel-flavored previews.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-4-Declare-an-event-mapper","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 4: Declare an event mapper"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The mapper is where you decide which actions become tracked events and what properties they carry. It runs in ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for every non-analytics action while the user is opted in.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxAnalytics","","let mapper = AnalyticsMapper<AppState, AppAction> { state, action in","    switch action {","    case .counter(.increment(let n)):","        return [AnalyticsEvent(\"counter_added\", [\"amount\": .int(n)])]","","    case .paywall(.request(let reason)):","        return [AnalyticsEvent(\"paywall_requested\", [\"reason\": .string(reason)])]","","    case .paywall(.customerInfoUpdated(let snapshot)) where snapshot.isPro:","        return [AnalyticsEvent(\"subscription_started\")]","","    default:","        return []","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A single action can produce zero, one, or several events. The mapper closure is allowed to read freely from ","type":"text"},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — that’s deliberately what gets passed in, post-reducer.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-5-Configure-auto-identify","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 5: Configure auto-identify"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your app has a stable userID source (e.g. an ","type":"text"},{"code":"auth.currentUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slice), let the plugin watch it. The plugin auto-fires ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on transitions and ","type":"text"},{"code":"reset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on sign-out, with no app-level plumbing.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let identity = AnalyticsIdentity<AppState>(","    userID: \\.auth.currentUserID,","    userProperties: { state in","        [","            \"subscription_tier\": state.paywall.isPro ? \"pro\" : \"free\",","            \"signup_date\": state.auth.signupDate.map(AnalyticsValue.date) ?? .null,","        ]","    }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is re-evaluated each non-analytics dispatch. The plugin re-fires ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whenever the returned dictionary changes — so derived people-properties (subscription tier, paywall entitlements, feature flags, A\/B variants) stay in sync with state without any explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":".identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plumbing.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-6-Wire-the-plugin","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 6: Wire the plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Construct and register ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxAnalytics","","let analyticsPlugin = AnalyticsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.analytics,","    action: AppAction.analytics,","    extractAction: { if case .analytics(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    service: MixpanelAnalyticsService(token: \"...\"),","    mapper: mapper,","    identity: identity",")","plugins.register(analyticsPlugin)"]},{"anchor":"Step-7-Track-screen-views","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 7: Track screen views"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dispatch ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics(.screenView(_:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from your view’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (or equivalent navigation hook). The plugin updates ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.analytics.currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and emits a ","type":"text"},{"code":"screen_view","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event with ","type":"text"},{"code":"screen_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus any extra properties.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct ProfileView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        Form { \/* … *\/ }","            .onAppear { store.send(.analytics(.screenView(\"Profile\"))) }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Subsequent mapper-emitted events are auto-enriched with ","type":"text"},{"code":"screen: \"Profile\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" until the next ","type":"text"},{"code":"screenView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" dispatch — useful for understanding ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"where","type":"text"}]},{"text":" an action originated without manually passing context through every event.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-8-Track-ad-hoc-events","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 8: Track ad-hoc events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For events that don’t map cleanly from a domain action, dispatch ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics(.track(_:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Button(\"Share\") {","    store.send(.analytics(.track(","        AnalyticsEvent(\"share_tapped\", [\"destination\": .string(\"twitter\")])","    )))","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This bypasses the mapper but still gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"currentScreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" auto-attached.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-9-Handle-opt-out","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 9: Handle opt-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Surface a privacy toggle that dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".analytics(.setOptedOut(_:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Toggle(\"Share usage analytics\", isOn: Binding(","    get: { !store.analytics.isOptedOut },","    set: { store.send(.analytics(.setOptedOut(!$0))) }","))"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"code":"setOptedOut(true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fires, the plugin clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"lastIdentifiedUserID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to clear server-side identity. While opted out, all tracking is dropped and auto-identify is paused. Opting back in re-identifies the user automatically on the next dispatch.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Engage-the-SDKs-own-consent-switch","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Engage the SDK’s own consent switch"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The gate above stops events Swidux dispatches. It does not tell your vendor’s SDK anything — so if that SDK collects automatic events, or is still holding its own queue, data can leave the device after the user opts out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your provider has a consent API, wire it through ","type":"text"},{"code":"onConsentChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when you build the plugin:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["AnalyticsPlugin(","    state: \\.analytics,","    action: AppAction.analytics,","    extractAction: { if case .analytics(let a) = $0 { a } else { nil } },","    service: mixpanel,","    onConsentChange: { optedOut in","        optedOut ? mixpanel.optOutTracking() : mixpanel.optInTracking()","    }",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The hook fires for either value, and on opt-out it runs before ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — so the SDK’s own opt-out closes the tap before the reset hands it an identity change that is still eligible to be sent. Events already in flight when the toggle fires are not retracted; the hook shuts off what happens next. This is the one place your app names the vendor, which the line constructing the service already does.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-10-Flush-on-app-shutdown","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 10: Flush on app shutdown"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the app moves to the background or terminates so in-flight events aren’t lost:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    @State private var store = AppStore.configured()","    @Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(store)","        }","        .onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","            if phase == .background {","                Task { await store.analyticsPlugin.flush() }","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" awaits any pending fire-and-forget service calls the plugin spawned, then calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"service.flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to drain the SDK’s own buffers.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Testing","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a recording ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to verify your mapper and explicit dispatches in tests:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Testing","@testable import SwiduxAnalytics","","actor RecordingAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    private(set) var events: [AnalyticsEvent] = []","    func track(_ event: AnalyticsEvent) async { events.append(event) }","    func identify(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]) async {}","    func alias(newID: String, previousID: String?) async {}","    func reset() async {}","    func flush() async {}","}","","@Test func incrementTracks() async {","    let service = RecordingAnalyticsService()","    let store = AppStore.configured(analyticsService: service)","","    store.send(.counter(.increment(5)))","    await store.analyticsPlugin.flush()","","    let events = await service.events","    #expect(events.first?.name == \"counter_added\")","    #expect(events.first?.properties[\"amount\"] == .int(5))","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the deterministic sync point — it awaits all pending tracking tasks before returning, so post-flush assertions are stable.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plumb the service through a parameter on your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory so previews and tests can override it without touching the live SDK.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Add Analytics","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]},{"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add a Parental Gate","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToCancelEffects":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects","title":"Cancel Effects"},"https://heirloomlogic.github.io/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/swiduxmixpanelanalytics/":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","title":"DocC reference","url":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC reference"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add a Version Killswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add a Paywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add iCloud Sync","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Add Feature Flags","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","title":"Add Persistence"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"}}}